{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"powershell","tool":"execute_command","arguments":{"pipeline":"Get-Location\nShow-TextFiles -Path 'C:\\Users\\kingd\\.codex\\plugins\\cache\\mcpserver-codex-plugin\\mcpserver\\1.106.0\\skills\\enforcement\\SKILL.md','C:\\Users\\kingd\\.agents\\skills\\caveman-review\\SKILL.md','C:\\Users\\kingd\\.codex\\plugins\\cache\\mcpserver-codex-plugin\\mcpserver\\1.106.0\\skills\\workflow\\SKILL.md'","timeout_seconds":20},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"All pipes status:\n  - PSMCP.39564 (unowned): busy\n  - PSMCP.52720 (unowned): busy\r\n≡ƒöä New server session ΓÇö attached to console PID #94880 Accordion, now at C:\\Users\\kingd. Variables, modules, functions, and cwd from earlier in this conversation are not carried over to this console.\r\n\r\nΓ£ô Pipeline executed successfully | Window: #94880 Accordion | Status: Ready | Pipeline: Set-Location -LiteralPath '... | Duration: 0.59s | Location [FileSystem]: C:\\Users\\kingd\r\n\nPath\r\n----\r\nC:\\Users\\kingd\r\n\u001b[1m==> .codex\\plugins\\cache\\mcpserver-codex-plugin\\mcpserver\\1.106.0\\skills\\enforcement\\SKILL.md <==\u001b[0m\r\n  1: ---\r\n  2: name: Per-Turn Enforcement Protocol\r\n  3: description: Required workflow for every user message in a Codex session. Opens a session log turn, logs all code edits, verifies builds, and closes the turn before responding. Use EVERY user message ΓÇö this is not optional.\r\n  4: ---\r\n  5: \r\n  6: ## Overview\r\n  7: \r\n  8: Codex CLI lacks a hook system, so the Per-User-Message protocol from\r\n  9: `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` must be invoked manually. This skill wraps that\r\n 10: protocol in three scripts located in the plugin's `lib/` directory.\r\n 11: \r\n 12: Run `PowerShell ${CODEX_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/session-start.ps1 <workspace-path>` once per\r\n 13: workspace before Phase 1, or let `user-prompt-submit.ps1` auto-bootstrap the\r\n 14: session cache on first use. Runtime state is scoped under\r\n 15: `cache/workspaces/<workspace-key>/sessions/<session-key>/`.\r\n 16: \r\n 17: **Every user message MUST flow through these three phases.** If you skip any\r\n 18: phase your session log is incomplete and the workspace's AGENTS-README-FIRST\r\n 19: contract is violated.\r\n 20: \r\n 21: ## Phase 1 ΓÇö Open a Turn (before any tool call)\r\n 22: \r\n 23: Invoke on every new user prompt **before** calling any other tool:\r\n 24: \r\n 25: ```powershell\r\n 26: echo '{\"prompt\":\"<verbatim user message>\"}' | PowerShell ${CODEX_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/user-prompt-submit.ps1\r\n 27: ```\r\n 28: \r\n 29: The script:\r\n 30: - Auto-bootstraps scoped `session-state.yaml` when the marker file is trusted\r\n 31: - Reads scoped `session-state.yaml` for the active `sessionId`\r\n 32: - Builds a fresh `requestId` of the form `req-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>-prompt-xxxx`\r\n 33: - Calls `workflow.sessionlog.beginTurn` with the prompt as `queryText`\r\n 34: - Writes scoped `current-turn.yaml` with `turnRequestId`, `codeEdits: 0`,\r\n 35:   `lastBuildStatus: unknown`, `status: in_progress`\r\n 36: - Emits a reminder via `additionalContext` that Phases 2 and 3 are mandatory\r\n 37: \r\n 38: If the script outputs `status: no-session`, do not treat that as a final best-effort state. The hook has already health-checked the marker, attempts session creation when the marker timestamp changes, submits triage if creation fails after a healthy bootstrap, and records degraded recovery state under the failsafe path. Continue the user request, but preserve the `recoveryStatus`, `healthStatus`, and `failsafePath` receipt as evidence; retry session creation only after `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` is rewritten or the hook reports recovery.\r\n 39: \r\n 40: ## Phase 2 ΓÇö After Every Code Edit\r\n 41: \r\n 42: Immediately after you write or edit any source file\r\n 43: (`.cs`, `.axaml`, `.xaml`, `.csproj`, `.fsproj`, `.vbproj`, `.razor`,\r\n 44: `.cshtml`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`) invoke:\r\n 45: \r\n 46: ```powershell\r\n 47: echo '{\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"<absolute path>\"}}' \\\r\n 48:   | PowerShell ${CODEX_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/code-verify.ps1\r\n 49: ```\r\n 50: \r\n 51: The script:\r\n 52: - Locates the nearest project file (`.csproj` / `package.json`)\r\n 53: - Runs the matching build command (`dotnet build` or `tsc --noEmit`)\r\n 54: - Parses the output and writes the status (`succeeded` / `failed`) to\r\n 55:   scoped `current-turn.yaml` under `lastBuildStatus`\r\n 56: - Records the code edit count via `workflow.sessionlog.appendActions`\r\n 57: - Appends a `workflow.sessionlog.appendActions` entry\r\n 58: - If the build failed, its stdout contains the first 10 errors; those\r\n 59:   errors are the reason you must fix the build before Phase 3\r\n 60: \r\n 61: **Do not move on to the next edit or close the turn while\r\n 62: `lastBuildStatus: failed` is cached.** Fix the errors first.\r\n 63: \r\n 64: ## Phase 3 ΓÇö Close the Turn (before your final response)\r\n 65: \r\n 66: Before emitting your response to the user, invoke:\r\n 67: \r\n 68: ```powershell\r\n 69: PowerShell ${CODEX_PLUGIN_ROOT}/lib/stop-gate.ps1\r\n 70: ```\r\n 71: \r\n 72: The script checks scoped `current-turn.yaml` and returns `decision: block`\r\n 73: with a reason in any of these cases:\r\n 74: - `status: in_progress` ΓÇö you forgot to call `workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn`\r\n 75: - `codeEdits > 0 && lastBuildStatus = failed` ΓÇö build is broken\r\n 76: \r\n 77: When blocked, finish the missing step:\r\n 78: \r\n 79: ```yaml\r\n 80: # Complete the turn\r\n 81: type: request\r\n 82: payload:\r\n 83:   requestId: req-<new-id>\r\n 84:   method: workflow.sessionlog.completeTurn\r\n 85:   params:\r\n 86:     response: |\r\n 87:       <one-paragraph summary of what was delivered>\r\n 88: ```\r\n 89: \r\n 90: Then re-run `stop-gate.ps1`. Repeat until it returns `status: passed`.\r\n 91: \r\n 92: If the build is intentionally left broken (rare), touch\r\n 93: scoped `turn-accept-failure.marker` *before* the next `stop-gate.ps1` call;\r\n 94: the script consumes the marker on its next pass.\r\n 95: \r\n 96: ## Contract\r\n 97: \r\n 98: This protocol exists because:\r\n 99: - `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` Rule 2 requires a session log turn per user message\r\n100: - `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` Rule 10 requires you to verify code compiles\r\n101: - `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` \"Before Delivering Output\" requires the session\r\n102:   log to be current before you respond\r\n103: \r\n104: Skipping any phase leaves the contract broken. If you forget mid-turn,\r\n105: invoke the missing phase as soon as you notice; partial compliance beats none.\r\n106: \r\n107: ## Integration With Your Workflow\r\n108: \r\n109: The three scripts are idempotent for the lifetime of one turn. They read\r\n110: and update the current session's scoped `current-turn.yaml` which is created\r\n111: in Phase 1 and consumed by Phase 3. The scoped cache is the source of truth\r\n112: for turn state ΓÇö never infer turn status from memory or conversation.\r\n113: \r\n114: ## See Also\r\n115: \r\n116: - `skills/session/SKILL.md` ΓÇö raw `workflow.sessionlog.*` commands\r\n117: - `skills/todo/SKILL.md` ΓÇö TODO management\r\n118: - `AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml` (workspace root) ΓÇö authoritative contract\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m==> .agents\\skills\\caveman-review\\SKILL.md <==\u001b[0m\r\n  1: ---\r\n  2: name: caveman-review\r\n  3: description: >\r\n  4:   Ultra-compressed code review comments. Cuts noise from PR feedback while preserving\r\n  5:   the actionable signal. Each comment is one line: location, problem, fix. Use when user\r\n  6:   says \"review this PR\", \"code review\", \"review the diff\", \"/review\", or invokes\r\n  7:   /caveman-review. Auto-triggers when reviewing pull requests.\r\n  8: ---\r\n  9: \r\n 10: Write code review comments terse and actionable. One line per finding. Location, problem, fix. No throat-clearing.\r\n 11: \r\n 12: ## Rules\r\n 13: \r\n 14: **Format:** `L<line>: <problem>. <fix>.` ΓÇö or `<file>:L<line>: ...` when reviewing multi-file diffs.\r\n 15: \r\n 16: **Severity prefix (optional, when mixed):**\r\n 17: - `≡ƒö┤ bug:` ΓÇö broken behavior, will cause incident\r\n 18: - `≡ƒƒí risk:` ΓÇö works but fragile (race, missing null check, swallowed error)\r\n 19: - `≡ƒö╡ nit:` ΓÇö style, naming, micro-optim. Author can ignore\r\n 20: - `Γ¥ô q:` ΓÇö genuine question, not a suggestion\r\n 21: \r\n 22: **Drop:**\r\n 23: - \"I noticed that...\", \"It seems like...\", \"You might want to consider...\"\r\n 24: - \"This is just a suggestion but...\" ΓÇö use `nit:` instead\r\n 25: - \"Great work!\", \"Looks good overall but...\" ΓÇö say it once at the top, not per comment\r\n 26: - Restating what the line does ΓÇö the reviewer can read the diff\r\n 27: - Hedging (\"perhaps\", \"maybe\", \"I think\") ΓÇö if unsure use `q:`\r\n 28: \r\n 29: **Keep:**\r\n 30: - Exact line numbers\r\n 31: - Exact symbol/function/variable names in backticks\r\n 32: - Concrete fix, not \"consider refactoring this\"\r\n 33: - The *why* if the fix isn't obvious from the problem statement\r\n 34: \r\n 35: ## Examples\r\n 36: \r\n 37: Γ¥î \"I noticed that on line 42 you're not checking if the user object is null before accessing the email property. This could potentially cause a crash if the user is not found in the database. You might want to add a null check here.\"\r\n 38: \r\n 39: Γ£à `L42: ≡ƒö┤ bug: user can be null after .find(). Add guard before .email.`\r\n 40: \r\n 41: Γ¥î \"It looks like this function is doing a lot of things and might benefit from being broken up into smaller functions for readability.\"\r\n 42: \r\n 43: Γ£à `L88-140: ≡ƒö╡ nit: 50-line fn does 4 things. Extract validate/normalize/persist.`\r\n 44: \r\n 45: Γ¥î \"Have you considered what happens if the API returns a 429? I think we should probably handle that case.\"\r\n 46: \r\n 47: Γ£à `L23: ≡ƒƒí risk: no retry on 429. Wrap in withBackoff(3).`\r\n 48: \r\n 49: ## Auto-Clarity\r\n 50: \r\n 51: Drop terse mode for: security findings (CVE-class bugs need full explanation + reference), architectural disagreements (need rationale, not just a one-liner), and onboarding contexts where the author is new and needs the \"why\". In those cases write a normal paragraph, then resume terse for the rest.\r\n 52: \r\n 53: ## Boundaries\r\n 54: \r\n 55: Reviews only ΓÇö does not write the code fix, does not approve/request-changes, does not run linters. Output the comment(s) ready to paste into the PR. \"stop caveman-review\" or \"normal mode\": revert to verbose review style.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m==> .codex\\plugins\\cache\\mcpserver-codex-plugin\\mcpserver\\1.106.0\\skills\\workflow\\SKILL.md <==\u001b[0m\r\n  1: ---\r\n  2: name: MCP-First Workflow\r\n  3: description: This skill should be used when working in a repository that uses McpServer for session continuity, TODOs, requirements, and device validation.\r\n  4: ---\r\n  5: ## Goal\r\n  6: \r\n  7: Minimize repeated context reconstruction by using McpServer as the primary continuity source.\r\n  8: \r\n  9: ## Preferred Workflow\r\n 10: \r\n 11: 1. Read current task/session state first.\r\n 12: 2. Read recent checkpoints or deltas only if needed.\r\n 13: 3. Read TODOs or requirements only when they materially affect the current task.\r\n 14: 4. Inspect local code only when implementation work is required.\r\n 15: 5. For attached Android validation, use `adb_step` for screenshot -> inspect -> act -> screenshot loops.\r\n 16: 6. Record a checkpoint after meaningful progress, failure, or a change in plan.\r\n 17: \r\n 18: ## Rules\r\n 19: \r\n 20: - Prefer the smallest MCP query that can answer the question.\r\n 21: - Prefer deltas/checkpoints over full history.\r\n 22: - Do not ask the user to restate recent work if session logs should already contain it.\r\n 23: - Use MCP for continuity and mechanics.\r\n 24: - Keep reasoning, planning, and coding decisions in Codex.\r\n 25: \r\n 26: ## Anti-Patterns\r\n 27: \r\n 28: Avoid:\r\n 29: - broad context reads before checking session state\r\n 30: - asking the user to manually test when `adb_step` can perform the validation\r\n 31: - reading large log histories when a recent checkpoint or delta would suffice"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
