{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"powershell","tool":"execute_command","arguments":{"pipeline":"Show-TextFiles -Path 'docs/requirements/functional/FR-RomM-Server.md' -First 85","timeout_seconds":20},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Γ£ô Pipeline executed successfully | Window: #94880 Accordion | Status: Ready | Pipeline: Show-TextFiles -Path 'docs/... | Duration: 0.67s | Location [FileSystem]: F:\\GitHub\\RomM\r\n\n\u001b[1m==> docs\\requirements\\functional\\FR-RomM-Server.md <==\u001b[0m\r\n  1: # RomM server functional requirements\r\n  2: \r\n  3: Source of behavior: operator RomM stack at `F:\\GitHub\\RomM` (thin `rommapp/romm` image plus CSDb bridge, GB64 import, HVSC bind). These FRs are the **server** contract ViceSharp clients consume. They are registered in the `vice-sharp-romm` MCP workspace.\r\n  4: \r\n  5: ## FR-ROMM-001: Structure A and built-in Commodore platforms\r\n  6: \r\n  7: The RomM stack shall treat upstream RomM as the library authority. Storage follows Structure A: `library/roms/{platform}/`. First-class Commodore roots use RomM built-in slugs only: `c64`, `c128`, `c-plus-4`, `vic-20`. Optional built-in slugs when present: `c16`, `cpet`, `commodore-cdtv`. Do not invent aliases (`plus4`, `vic20`) as folder names.\r\n  8: \r\n  9: Acceptance:\r\n 10: \r\n 11: 1. Host `runtime/library/roms/` uses only RomM slugs.\r\n 12: 2. Empty platform folders created on first run persist across container recreate.\r\n 13: 3. Custom side folders remap via `config.yml` `system.platforms` to a built-in slug or are retired.\r\n 14: \r\n 15: ## FR-ROMM-002: Distinct C64, C128, Plus/4, and VIC-20 libraries\r\n 16: \r\n 17: The operator library shall include distinct Structure A trees `roms/c64/`, `roms/c128/`, `roms/c-plus-4/`, and `roms/vic-20/`. Content is placed in the platform that matches the software. Host paths under `runtime/library/roms/{slug}/` exist and are bind-mounted.\r\n 18: \r\n 19: Acceptance:\r\n 20: \r\n 21: 1. Compose up lists those four directories on host and at `/romm/library/roms/`.\r\n 22: 2. A probe file under host `roms/vic-20/` is visible in the container at the matching path.\r\n 23: 3. VIC-20 or Plus/4 titles are not dumped into `c64`.\r\n 24: \r\n 25: ## FR-ROMM-003: Preserve config on redeploy\r\n 26: \r\n 27: Redeploy shall preserve `.env`, `runtime/config/config.yml`, `runtime/assets`, `runtime/library`, `runtime/csdb`, host HVSC, and `gb64`. `Prepare-RomMLibrary.ps1` never overwrites a non-empty `config.yml`. GB64 game import and screenshot sync run only when the corresponding attached library data is missing, unless `--ForceLibraryBuild`.\r\n 28: \r\n 29: Acceptance:\r\n 30: \r\n 31: 1. Existing non-empty `config.yml` is byte-identical after redeploy.\r\n 32: 2. Populated `roms/c64` or marker `.gb64-library-built` skips game import (prepare reports SKIP).\r\n 33: 3. Empty `roms/c64` plus present `gb64/Games` runs `Gb64Import`.\r\n 34: 4. Populated `library/screenshots` or marker `.screenshots-synced` skips screenshot robocopy.\r\n 35: \r\n 36: ## FR-ROMM-004: HVSC and screenshots on the attached library\r\n 37: \r\n 38: NFO `SID:` and `Screenshot:` relative paths resolve against attached library roots: `library/hvsc` and `library/screenshots` under `runtime/library` (container `/romm/library`). HVSC is not baked into the image and is not a RomM platform under `roms/`.\r\n 39: \r\n 40: Acceptance:\r\n 41: \r\n 42: 1. Compose mounts `./runtime/library` to `/romm/library` including both roots.\r\n 43: 2. `Resolve-SidPath` finds a fixture SID under `library/hvsc`.\r\n 44: 3. `Resolve-ScreenshotPath` finds `Letter/file.png` under `library/screenshots`.\r\n 45: \r\n 46: ## FR-ROMM-005: REST heartbeat and authentication\r\n 47: \r\n 48: The RomM HTTP API on port 8080 shall expose `GET /api/heartbeat` and accept authenticated calls with `Authorization: Bearer` (client token `rmm_...`) or the documented OAuth/password flow. Tokens must not appear in URL query strings. Unauthenticated protected routes return 401.\r\n 49: \r\n 50: Acceptance:\r\n 51: \r\n 52: 1. Heartbeat returns a JSON health payload without requiring a ROM download.\r\n 53: 2. Bearer token is sent on protected `/api/*` calls.\r\n 54: 3. 401 is returned when the token is missing or invalid.\r\n 55: \r\n 56: ## FR-ROMM-006: Platforms API\r\n 57: \r\n 58: `GET /api/platforms` shall list platforms with numeric id and slug. `GET /api/platforms/{id}` shall return one platform. Slugs include `c64`, `c128`, `c-plus-4`, `vic-20` when those libraries exist.\r\n 59: \r\n 60: Acceptance:\r\n 61: \r\n 62: 1. List returns JSON objects with `id` and `slug`.\r\n 63: 2. Slug `c64` (and the other required slugs when present) can be resolved to a numeric id.\r\n 64: 3. Get-by-id matches list.\r\n 65: \r\n 66: ## FR-ROMM-007: ROM list, search, page, and char index\r\n 67: \r\n 68: `GET /api/roms` shall support `search_term`, `platform_ids`, `limit`, `offset`, `order_by`, `order_dir`. The page payload shall include items, total, offset, and a character index suitable for A-Z jump.\r\n 69: \r\n 70: Acceptance:\r\n 71: \r\n 72: 1. `platform_ids` scopes results to that platform.\r\n 73: 2. `search_term` filters by name.\r\n 74: 3. `limit`/`offset` page the result.\r\n 75: 4. Response includes total and a char index map for letters that have titles.\r\n 76: \r\n 77: ## FR-ROMM-008: ROM detail\r\n 78: \r\n 79: `GET /api/roms/{id}` shall return detailed ROM metadata including files (`fs_name`), cover fields, summary, and enough data to decide launchability.\r\n 80: \r\n 81: Acceptance:\r\n 82: \r\n 83: 1. Detail includes at least one file with `fs_name` when the ROM has content.\r\n 84: 2. Cover URL or path fields are present when artwork exists.\r\n 85: 3. Unknown id returns 404."}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
