{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"powershell","tool":"execute_command","arguments":{"pipeline":"Show-TextFiles -Path 'docs/requirements/technical/TR-RomM-Server.md' -First 62\nShow-TextFiles -Path 'docs/requirements/test/TEST-RomM-Server.md' -First 29\nrg -n 'TEST-AUTH|TR-AUTH|TR-ERR|FR-AUTH|FR-ROM-00|Acceptance|AC-|acId|acceptanceCriteria' docs/Project/wiki/azure docs/Project/wiki/github -g '*Requirements.md' -g '*Mapping.md'","timeout_seconds":20},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Γ£ô Pipeline executed successfully | Window: #94880 Accordion | Status: Ready | Pipeline: Show-TextFiles -Path 'docs/... | Duration: 0.55s | Location [FileSystem]: F:\\GitHub\\RomM\r\n\n\u001b[1m==> docs\\requirements\\technical\\TR-RomM-Server.md <==\u001b[0m\r\n  1: # RomM server technical requirements\r\n  2: \r\n  3: ## TR-ROMM-STRUCT-001: Structure A layout\r\n  4: \r\n  5: RomM storage is `runtime/library/roms/{slug}/` on the host, `/romm/library/roms/{slug}/` in the container. docker-compose binds `./runtime/library` to `/romm/library`.\r\n  6: \r\n  7: ## TR-ROMM-PLAT-001: Built-in Commodore slugs\r\n  8: \r\n  9: Use exact slugs `c64`, `c128`, `c-plus-4`, `vic-20`. Optional: `c16`, `cpet`, `commodore-cdtv`. config.yml must not redefine those identities. Temporary `c64-csdb-*` folders remap to `c64`.\r\n 10: \r\n 11: ## TR-ROMM-CFG-001: config.yml remaps only when needed\r\n 12: \r\n 13: Preferred end state: no staging folders. If staging remains, each remap target is a built-in slug.\r\n 14: \r\n 15: ## TR-ROMM-DEPLOY-001: Preserve-and-prepare\r\n 16: \r\n 17: Deploy stashes and restores `.env`, `runtime/config`, `runtime/library`, `runtime/assets`, `runtime/csdb`, `hvsc`, `gb64`. `Prepare-RomMLibrary.ps1` creates required platform dirs and imports GB64 only when `roms/c64` lacks media.\r\n 18: \r\n 19: ## TR-ROMM-MEDIA-001: HVSC and screenshot roots\r\n 20: \r\n 21: `HVSC_ROOT=/romm/library/hvsc`, `SCREENSHOTS_ROOT=/romm/library/screenshots`. csdb-bridge uses `/data/library/hvsc` and `/data/library/screenshots` on the same host bind. Dockerfile does not bake HVSC.\r\n 22: \r\n 23: ## TR-ROMM-API-001: Pinned REST surface\r\n 24: \r\n 25: Server HTTP is RomM 5.x compatible with the pinned snapshot `openapi/romm-5.0.0.json` in `F:\\GitHub\\RomM`. Required paths: `/api/heartbeat`, `/api/platforms`, `/api/platforms/{id}`, `/api/roms`, `/api/roms/{id}`, ROM content download, tasks/scan, collections. JSON field names match `RomM.Client` (`search_term`, `platform_ids`, `fs_name`, `url_cover`, `char_index` when advertised).\r\n 26: \r\n 27: ## TR-ROMM-AUTH-001: Bearer and 401\r\n 28: \r\n 29: Protected `/api` routes require `Authorization: Bearer`. Client tokens use the `rmm_` prefix when issued as API keys. Tokens never appear in query strings. 401 on missing/invalid credentials.\r\n 30: \r\n 31: ## TR-ROMM-COLL-001: Collections REST\r\n 32: \r\n 33: Collections use `/api/collections` with scopes `collections.read` / `collections.write`. Mutating a smart/virtual collection is rejected.\r\n 34: \r\n 35: ## TR-CSDB-ARCH-001: CSDb sidecar, not a RomM fork\r\n 36: \r\n 37: CSDb is `csdb-bridge` (ASP.NET) on :8090 and/or in-process `RomM.Client.Csdb`. Do not fork RomM Python core. Share Structure A `LIBRARY_ROMS_ROOT`.\r\n 38: \r\n 39: ## TR-CSDB-INGEST-001: Ingest pipeline\r\n 40: \r\n 41: `POST /csdb/v1/ingest` accepts 1..20 `{kind, csdb_id}` items. Extract archives. Rate-limit CSDb HTTP. Optional RomM scan after write.\r\n 42: \r\n 43: ## TR-HVSC-HOST-001: Host HVSC tool\r\n 44: \r\n 45: `scripts/Download-Hvsc.ps1` and `tools/HvscFetch` write to `runtime/library/hvsc` by default.\r\n 46: \r\n 47: ## TR-GB64-IMPORT-001: C# Gb64Import\r\n 48: \r\n 49: Game import is `tools/Gb64Import` (.NET), invoked by prepare via `dotnet run --project tools/Gb64Import`. No Python. Args: `--games`, `--out`, `--hvsc`, `--screenshots`, `--force`, `--limit`, `--fix-sids`, `--validate-assets`, `--dry-run`. Media extensions for \"has library media\" include d64/g64/t64/tap/crt/prg/p00/sid/zip/7z/rar.\r\n 50: \r\n 51: ## TR-GB64-TAG-001: Tag mapping from VERSION.NFO\r\n 52: \r\n 53: Filename/folder tags follow `docs/gb64-romm-tag-mapping.md` and `RomTagBuilder`: Unique-ID `(gb64-{id})`, GB-Version `(rev-NN)`, Language split on `/`, Pal/NTSC to region+video tags, True Drive Emul. Yes -> `(TrueDrive)`. ZIP stem `{SHORTNAME}_{id}_{rev}.zip` supplies fallback id/rev.\r\n 54: \r\n 55: ## TR-GB64-STATE-001: Import resume and markers\r\n 56: \r\n 57: Importer state file `.gb64-import-state.txt` under `roms/c64` (Unique-ID per line). Prepare game marker `roms/.gb64-library-built`. Screenshot marker `library/screenshots/.screenshots-synced`. Force clears import state.\r\n 58: \r\n 59: ## TR-GB64-SIDFIX-001: SID field repair\r\n 60: \r\n 61: `SidNfoFixer` builds an HVSC basename index and rewrites NFO `SID:` inside GB64 ZIPs (remap or `(None)`). Receipt at `runtime/library/sid-nfo-fix-receipt.txt` unless overridden.\r\n 62: \r\n\u001b[1m==> docs\\requirements\\test\\TEST-RomM-Server.md <==\u001b[0m\r\n  1: # RomM server test requirements\r\n  2: \r\n  3: ## TEST-ROMM-001: Platform directories\r\n  4: \r\n  5: On a running stack, `/romm/library/roms` contains `c64`, `c128`, `c-plus-4`, and `vic-20` (empty allowed). HVSC is at `/romm/library/hvsc`, not under `roms/`. Docs and compose do not use `plus4` or `vic20` as folder names.\r\n  6: \r\n  7: ## TEST-ROMM-002: Bind persistence\r\n  8: \r\n  9: A probe file under host `roms/vic-20/` is visible at `/romm/library/roms/vic-20/` in the container.\r\n 10: \r\n 11: ## TEST-ROMM-003: Redeploy skip/import\r\n 12: \r\n 13: Existing `config.yml` plus populated `roms/c64` leaves config byte-identical and skips GB64 import. Empty `roms/c64` plus `gb64/Games` runs library build.\r\n 14: \r\n 15: ## TEST-ROMM-004: SID and screenshot path resolution\r\n 16: \r\n 17: Fixture HVSC and screenshot trees under `runtime/library` resolve NFO relative paths. Compose has a single library bind.\r\n 18: \r\n 19: ## TEST-ROMM-005: REST contract\r\n 20: \r\n 21: Against a running RomM (or recorded fixtures matching OpenAPI 5.0.0): heartbeat, platforms list/get, roms list with `platform_ids`/`search_term`/`limit`/`offset`, rom detail, authenticated download, scan task start/status. Covered in `F:\\GitHub\\RomM\\tests\\RomM.Client.Tests` (`RomMCoreClientTests`, `OpenApiCoverageTests`, `RomListQueryTests`).\r\n 22: \r\n 23: ## TEST-ROMM-006: Collections\r\n 24: \r\n 25: List/create/add/remove/rename/delete collections; smart collections are read-only.\r\n 26: \r\n 27: ## TEST-GB64-001: GB64 organizer landing\r\n 28: \r\n 29: Packages land under `roms/c64` with `(gb64-{id})` tags, never letter-bucket parents. `tools/Gb64Import.Tests`.\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/azure\\Technical-Requirements.md:3:## TR-AUTH-001\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/azure\\Technical-Requirements.md:5:**TR-AUTH-001** ΓÇö Placeholder requirement backfilled for TODO link TR-AUTH-001.\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/azure\\Technical-Requirements.md:55:## TR-ERR-001\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/azure\\Technical-Requirements.md:57:**TR-ERR-001** ΓÇö Placeholder requirement backfilled for TODO link TR-ERR-001.\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/github\\Technical-Requirements.md:3:## TR-AUTH-001\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/github\\Technical-Requirements.md:5:**TR-AUTH-001** ΓÇö Placeholder requirement backfilled for TODO link TR-AUTH-001.\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/github\\Technical-Requirements.md:55:## TR-ERR-001\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/github\\Technical-Requirements.md:57:**TR-ERR-001** ΓÇö Placeholder requirement backfilled for TODO link TR-ERR-001.\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/github\\Functional-Requirements.md:3:## FR-AUTH-001 FR-AUTH-001\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/github\\Functional-Requirements.md:5:Placeholder requirement backfilled for TODO link FR-AUTH-001.\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/github\\Functional-Requirements.md:8:## FR-AUTH-002 FR-AUTH-002\r\ndocs/Project/wiki/github\\Functional-Requirements.md:10:Placeholder requirement backf