{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"powershell","tool":"execute_command","arguments":{"pipeline":"[pscustomobject]@{PowerShell=$PSVersionTable.PSVersion.ToString();Runtime=[System.Runtime.InteropServices.RuntimeInformation]::FrameworkDescription} | ConvertTo-Json\nShow-TextFiles -Path 'F:\\GitHub\\McpServer\\docs\\Development-Process-draft-v4.md' -Skip 34 -First 22\nShow-TextFiles -Path 'tests/RomM.Client.Tests/TestHttpHandlers.cs'\nGet-Item -LiteralPath 'docs/Project/wiki/github/Functional-Requirements.md','docs/Project/wiki/azure/Functional-Requirements.md' | Select-Object FullName,LastWriteTimeUtc\nrg -n 'Roms.GetAsync|DetailedRom|char_index|WithFiles|Cancellation|Concurrent|Task.WhenAll|Skip\\s*=|Explicit\\s*=' tests/RomM.Client.Tests\nGet-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 -LiteralPath 'openapi/romm-5.0.0.json','tests/RomM.Client.Tests/bin/Release/net10.0/RomM.Client.Tests.dll'","timeout_seconds":20},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Γ£ô Pipeline executed successfully | Window: #94880 Accordion | Status: Ready | Pipeline: [pscustomobject]@{PowerShel... | Duration: 0.64s | Location [FileSystem]: F:\\GitHub\\RomM\r\n\n{\r\n  \"PowerShell\": \"7.6.5\",\r\n  \"Runtime\": \".NET 10.0.11\"\r\n}\r\n\u001b[1m==> ..\\McpServer\\docs\\Development-Process-draft-v4.md <==\u001b[0m\r\n 35: \r\n 36: When an agent enters a new workspace, the first step is a simple, guided handshake:\r\n 37: \r\n 38: - It performs an immediate health check on the MCP Server.\r\n 39: - It verifies a cryptographic signature embedded directly in the workspaceΓÇÖs agents-readme-first.yaml file.\r\n 40: - It issues a one-time nonce challenge to confirm the server is live and responsive.\r\n 41: \r\n 42: Only after these quick, deterministic checks pass does the agent proceed to load or create a session log and begin using the full suite of persistent context tools. If any part of the handshake fails, the agent is explicitly instructed to log ΓÇ£MCP_UNTRUSTEDΓÇ¥ and gracefully fall back to its internal memory ΓÇö no probing, no risk, no wasted cycles.\r\n 43: \r\n 44: This approach gives every model a clear, repeatable way to validate the integrity of the environment before committing resources. It transforms the MCP Server from an external dependency into a trusted partner that the agent can confidently rely on session after session. Once trust is established, the exponential productivity gains youΓÇÖve already observed become the norm rather than the exception.\r\n 45: \r\n 46: > The handshake is not extra ceremony ΓÇö it is the foundation that turns a collection of stateless models into a reliable, persistent development team.\r\n 47: \r\n 48: ## The Byrd Software Development Life Cycle\r\n 49: \r\n 50: Of well-known SDLC methodologies, this process is most closely related to the Rational Unified Process (RUP).  It follows the same iterative-rapids (a series of mini-waterfalls) as RUP, but incorporates strong boundaries for dependency tracking and management and risk mitigation by prioritizing testability and proof over raw efficiency.  Similar to operating a motor vehicle, going faster is often counter-productive when risks are not managed and cause delays when things go sideways out of a lack of respect for the seriousness of the consequences of those mistakes.  Spotting mistakes and correcting them early is always better than spotting them late when they cannot be corrected without great harm or expense.\r\n 51: \r\n 52: At its foundation, this development process rests on a hybrid worldview of intelligence. While AI models operate according to fundamentally deterministic principles ΓÇö functioning as pure, stateless computations governed by fixed weights ΓÇö genuine creativity, agency, and adaptive problem-solving emerge at the macro level through intentional Human guidance, persistent external context via the MCP Server, and well-designed processes. This combination allows us to harness the precision and perseverance of deterministic systems while unlocking the emergent intelligence and intuition that only arise through thoughtful Human-AI collaboration.\r\n 53: \r\n 54: ### Planning\r\n 55: \r\n 56: The justification for building software comes from one of two motivations.  Software can be a form of expressive art, such as a demonstration, a learning exercise, or even creating a homebrew game for enjoyment by the creator and/or others.  More typically, software is created to solve problems associated with performing work.  Defining that work and the problems to solve, the known environmental realities, and the intended users that benefit from the software solving the problems is critical in creating _viable_ and _valuable_ software.\r\n\u001b[1m==> tests\\RomM.Client.Tests\\TestHttpHandlers.cs <==\u001b[0m\r\n  1: using System.Net;\r\n  2: \r\n  3: namespace RomM.Client.Tests;\r\n  4: \r\n  5: /// <summary>Records outbound requests and returns scripted responses for auth tests.</summary>\r\n  6: internal sealed class RecordingHttpMessageHandler : HttpMessageHandler\r\n  7: {\r\n  8:     private readonly Func<HttpRequestMessage, int, CancellationToken, Task<HttpResponseMessage>> _responder;\r\n  9:     private int _callIndex;\r\n 10: \r\n 11:     public RecordingHttpMessageHandler(\r\n 12:         Func<HttpRequestMessage, int, CancellationToken, Task<HttpResponseMessage>>? responder = null)\r\n 13:     {\r\n 14:         _responder = responder ?? ((_, _, _) =>\r\n 15:             Task.FromResult(new HttpResponseMessage(HttpStatusCode.OK)\r\n 16:             {\r\n 17:                 Content = new StringContent(\"{}\"),\r\n 18:             }));\r\n 19:     }\r\n 20: \r\n 21:     public List<RecordedRequest> Requests { get; } = new();\r\n 22: \r\n 23:     protected override async Task<HttpResponseMessage> SendAsync(\r\n 24:         HttpRequestMessage request,\r\n 25:         CancellationToken cancellationToken)\r\n 26:     {\r\n 27:         var index = Interlocked.Increment(ref _callIndex) - 1;\r\n 28:         var auth = request.Headers.Authorization;\r\n 29:         var body = request.Content is null\r\n 30:             ? null\r\n 31:             : await request.Content.ReadAsStringAsync(cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\r\n 32: \r\n 33:         Requests.Add(new RecordedRequest(\r\n 34:             request.Method,\r\n 35:             request.RequestUri,\r\n 36:             auth?.Scheme,\r\n 37:             auth?.Parameter,\r\n 38:             body,\r\n 39:             request.Content?.Headers.ContentType?.MediaType));\r\n 40: \r\n 41:         return await _responder(request, index, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\r\n 42:     }\r\n 43: }\r\n 44: \r\n 45: internal sealed record RecordedRequest(\r\n 46:     HttpMethod Method,\r\n 47:     Uri? RequestUri,\r\n 48:     string? AuthScheme,\r\n 49:     string? AuthParameter,\r\n 50:     string? Body,\r\n 51:     string? ContentType);\r\n 52: \r\n 53: /// <summary>Fixed-status inner handler for exception-mapping tests.</summary>\r\n 54: internal sealed class FixedStatusHandler : HttpMessageHandler\r\n 55: {\r\n 56:     private readonly HttpStatusCode _status;\r\n 57:     private readonly string _body;\r\n 58: \r\n 59:     public FixedStatusHandler(HttpStatusCode status, string body = \"\")\r\n 60:     {\r\n 61:         _status = status;\r\n 62:         _body = body;\r\n 63:     }\r\n 64: \r\n 65:     protected override Task<HttpResponseMessage> SendAsync(\r\n 66:         HttpRequestMessage request,\r\n 67:         CancellationToken cancellationToken)\r\n 68:     {\r\n 69:         var response = new HttpResponseMessage(_status)\r\n 70:         {\r\n 71:             Content = new StringContent(_body),\r\n 72:             RequestMessage = request,\r\n 73:         };\r\n 74:         return Task.FromResult(response);\r\n 75:     }\r\n 76: }\r\n\r\nFullName                                                           LastWriteTimeUtc\r\n--------                                                           ----------------\r\nF:\\GitHub\\RomM\\docs\\Project\\wiki\\github\\Functional-Requirements.md 9/15/2026 9:05:21 PM\r\nF:\\GitHub\\RomM\\docs\\Project\\wiki\\azure\\Functional-Requirements.md  9/15/2026 9:05:21 PM\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\CsdbClientTests.cs:106:        protected override Task<HttpResponseMessage> SendAsync(HttpRequestMessage request, CancellationToken cancellationToken)\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\CsdbClientTests.cs:120:        protected override Task<HttpResponseMessage> SendAsync(HttpRequestMessage request, CancellationToken cancellationToken) =>\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\CsdbIngestAndWorkflowTests.cs:250:        public Task<IReadOnlyList<CsdbSearchHit>> SearchAsync(CsdbSearchRequest request, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) =>\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\CsdbIngestAndWorkflowTests.cs:253:        public Task<CsdbReleaseDetail> GetReleaseAsync(int csdbId, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\CsdbIngestAndWorkflowTests.cs:271:        public Task<CsdbSidDetail> GetSidAsync(int csdbId, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\CsdbIngestAndWorkflowTests.cs:281:        public Task<(byte[] Data, string? FileName)> DownloadBytesAsync(string url, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\CsdbIngestAndWorkflowTests.cs:298:        protected override Task<HttpResponseMessage> SendAsync(HttpRequestMessage request, CancellationToken cancellationToken) =>\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\TestHttpHandlers.cs:8:    private readonly Func<HttpRequestMessage, int, CancellationToken, Task<HttpResponseMessage>> _responder;\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\TestHttpHandlers.cs:12:        Func<HttpRequestMessage, int, CancellationToken, Task<HttpResponseMessage>>? responder = null)\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\TestHttpHandlers.cs:25:        CancellationToken cancellationToken)\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\TestHttpHandlers.cs:67:        CancellationToken cancellationToken)\r\ntests/RomM.Client.Tests\\RomMCoreClientTests.cs:221:            CancellationToken cancellationToken) =>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
